This product includes software developed for the open implementation of the
ideal-mixing-of-complex-components (IMCC) model for silicate melt speciation.

Datapacks, benchmark sets and validation decks distributed with this software
are licensed separately under CC-BY-4.0; see LICENSE-DATA.

The thermodynamic coefficients in those datapacks derive from published work by
their respective authors, recorded per row with a provenance class. Principal
sources:

  Fegley B., Cameron A.G.W. (1987) Earth Planet. Sci. Lett. 82, 207-222.
    doi:10.1016/0012-821X(87)90196-8
  Schaefer L., Fegley B. (2004) Icarus 169, 216-241.
    doi:10.1016/j.icarus.2003.11.023
  NIST-JANAF Thermochemical Tables (public domain).

Users of a datapack should cite the underlying source in addition to this
software.
